{{also|addon|add on}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|addon}}

===Etymology===
From the verb phrase {{m|en|add on}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something which can be appended to something else.
# {{lb|en|computer hardware|software}} A [[software]] extension or [[hardware]] [[peripheral]] that provides additional functions or customization for a core application or system.
#* '''2010''', Kenneth Baldauf, Ralph Stair, ''Succeeding with Technology'' (page 77)
#*: Microdrives that can hold several gigabytes (see Figure 2.20) have been available as '''add-ons''' for portable devices.
# {{lb|en|poker}} Additional [[chip]]s that can be [[purchase]]d at specific times in tournament play.

